  "verdict": "allowed",
  "section": "37",
  "quote": "A notice of termination need not be given if a landlord and a tenant have agreed to terminate a tenancy.",
  "reason": "Section 37(3) of the Residential Tenancies Act, 2006 expressly allows a landlord and tenant to terminate a tenancy by mutual agreement without giving a notice of termination, while section 37(5) only voids agreements to terminate that are entered into at the time the tenancy agreement is made."
}

